   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "diva_balance_step4",
     "description": "The DIVA momentum balance on the converged FE solution of step 4 at the three interior vertices (3,3), (4,4), (2,5) = global (26,16), (27,17), (25,18). Chain pins: the imported-by-reference slope-correction chain (z_mean = usrf - thck/2 -> plain vertex gradient cism_stag_vertex_gradient_x/y -> theta = atan(|dz|) -> F = cos^2(theta) + 4 sin^2(theta) -> beta_eff = F*beta/(F + beta*omega*cos(theta)), the same cism_templates.esm laws the stage-2 velocity lane applies at the traced cells) pinned STRAIGHT TO THE DUMPED CSV COLUMNS stag_diva_slope_factor_x/y and beta_eff_x/y at rel 1e-12 (stage1/dumps/cism/cism_velo_patch.csv, step-4 VERT rows at the pinned vertices). The eight membrane terms T1x..T4y and the exact sums are deliberately NOT pinned: they are not dump columns, so a pin would compare the model against a Python transcription of the same stencil (tautological); they are covered through the sums below. Residual pins: Rx = T1x+T2x+T3x+T4x - beta_eff_x*uvel_2d + taudx and Ry likewise are FAILABLE (every term is computed from the overridden fields), and each is asserted |R| <= 1.5% of the largest local term AND |Rx| <= 1.5%*|taudx| / |Ry| <= 1.5%*|taudy| (the driving-stress check: R = membrane + basal - driving is measured against CESM's own dumped driving stress; the FE solver converged to 1e-7 relative, which_ho_resid = HO_RESID_L2NORM_RELATIVE = 4, but the FD operator is NOT the FE assembly - 9-point bilinear stencil with quad-point integration vs the face fluxes - so the measured FE-vs-FD residual is 0.16-0.80% of the largest local term and 0.16-1.18% of the driving stress at these vertices, and the 1.5% tolerance is about 2x the measured maximum; anywhere in the interior the residual is up to 0.6% of the patch-wide driving-stress scale; see README.md).",
